<<<
+ heteroclite (Gram.); second declension’. Greek & Latin nouns having forms belonging to more than one declension, as Latin domus (gen. pl. domuum 4th, domorum 2nd), are called h.
===
*heteroclite* (Gram.); 'having a second declension'. Greek & Latin nouns having forms belonging to more than one declension, as Latin *domus* (gen. pl. *domuum* 4th, *domorum* 2nd), are called h.
>>>

<<<
hexameter (Pros.); ' six-measure '. The Greek & Latin heroic metre, in full dactylic h. acataiectic, on the scheme with a caesura (see above).
===
*hexameter* (Pros.); 'six-measure'. The Greek & Latin heroic metre, in full *dactylic h. acatalectic*, on the scheme

	—⏑⏑/—⏑⏑/—⏑⏑/—⏑⏑/—⏑⏑/—⏑
	——/——/——/——/ /——

with a *caesura* (see above).
>>>

