used in elegiacs (see above). tated in modern languages, e.g. by Goethe in Hermann und Dorothea, by Longfellow in Evangeline & Miles Standish, & by Clough in The Bothie & elsewhere. Chanced it my/eye fell a/side on a/

capless /bonnetless /maiden Bending with/three-pronged /fork in

a/garden up/rooting po/tatoes.
===
Also used in *elegiacs* (see above). Imitated in modern languages, e.g. by Goethe in *Hermann und Dorothea*, by Longfellow in *Evangeline* & *Miles Standish*, & by Clough in *The Bothie* & elsewhere.

	Chanced it my/eye fell a/side on a/capless/bonnetless/maiden
	Bending with/three-pronged/fork in a/garden up/rooting po/tatoes.
>>>

